<title>ITALY: Italy's apricot, plum crops badly hit by frost.</title>
<headline>Italy's apricot, plum crops badly hit by frost.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heavy damage caused by frost will result in a sharp fall in Italy's apricot and plum harvests this year, the Italian Institute for Agricultural Research (Ismea) said.</p>
<p>The apricot crop is estimated 10 percent lower at 125,000 tonnes and plum production will be 17 percent down at 150,000 tonnes, Ismea said in a statement.</p>
<p>Emilia Romagna region was particularly badly hit, with apricots down by over 17 percent to 36,000 tonnes and plums by almost 20 percent to 62,000 tonnes.</p>
</text>
